{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>In those days I was mourning three weeks of days.</b> This was in the month of Nisan. How did he mourn during the days of Hag HaMatzot and not drink wine on the night of Pesach, the night of the fifteenth? For it is written: \"for from the first day that you set your heart to fast before Elohim\" — and I come with your words in the commandment of HaShem, for so it is written: \"for now I have sent you.\" Only the prince of the king of Persia stood against me twenty-one days, which are the three weeks that you fasted. Therefore I said to come, and were it not for Michael who helped me, I would still have been there in the war with the kings of Persia. And now, when I return from you, I shall return to fight with the prince of Persia. And this was on the twenty-fourth of the first month. Only we do not know this month, whether it is the month of Nisan or it is the first month of the third year of the kingdom of Cyrus, in the manner of \"the twenty-fifth year of our exile, at the beginning of the year\" — and behold, this is on the tenth of the fifth month, for on it the House was burned."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The comment weaves together quotations and allusions from Daniel 10, Ezra, and Ezekiel without explicit markers between them; the seams are preserved as in the original. 'The House was burned' refers to the Temple."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:45.808573042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}